{"chunk_id": "9601d99a4088", "text": "Yudhishthira asks the sage Markandeya to recount the story of Vaivaswata Manu. Markandeya describes Manu performing immense austerities when a small fish begs him for protection from larger fish. Moved by compassion, Manu keeps transferring the rapidly growing fish from a pot to a tank, then to the Ganga, and finally to the sea. The fish then reveals an approaching cosmic deluge that will destroy the world and instructs Manu to build an ark, gather the seven sages and the seeds of all life, and await its return. When the flood comes, the horned fish tows Manu\u2019s ark across the endless waters until it is tied to a Himalayan peak. The fish reveals itself as Brahma, who has preserved life so creation can begin anew.\nMarkandeya recounts how Manu rescues a fish who warns of a coming cosmic flood and guides an ark carrying sages and seeds to safety.\nThemes: cosmic flood myth, divine intervention, preservation of life, Manu and creation, avatar of Brahma", "vector": [0.01337213534861803, -0.028082160279154778, -0.0050474912859499454, 0.01373701449483633, -0.020244020968675613, 0.00804084911942482, -0.041488081216812134, -0.005385342054069042, -0.018879104405641556, -0.009263869374990463, 0.0037467656657099724, 0.008635466918349266, 0.015554651618003845, 0.015460053458809853, 0.01063554361462593, -0.010013897903263569, 0.03524459898471832, -0.0037231161259114742, 0.008398971520364285, -0.027149692177772522, -0.009290897287428379, 0.008905747905373573, 0.0082097752019763, 0.002815986517816782, -0.01832502894103527, 0.004236649256199598, 0.03583921492099762, -0.025082044303417206, 0.011128806509077549, -0.026190195232629776, -0.0027264561504125595, -0.005179252941161394, 0.0013953238958492875, -0.0018395977094769478, -0.025555036962032318, 0.015027604065835476, 0.0011588282650336623, -0.004908972419798374, 0.02486582100391388, -0.018811533227562904, 0.01870342157781124, 0.0011765655362978578, -0.015554651618003845, 0.022487349808216